{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1091310-norse-courts-or-a-dude-trying-to-make-a-stable-freehold-with-dawn-and-dusk","id":1091310,"title":"Norse Courts. Or: a dude trying to make a stable freehold with Dawn and Dusk.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-11T15:48:25-07:00","id":1091310,"title":"Norse Courts. Or: a dude trying to make a stable freehold with Dawn and Dusk.","content":"So, my dark secret is revealed: I really like the Dawn and Dusk court.<br /> A bit of it comes from my family's proud research into our Norse heritage, and a bit of it is that I can really admire the duality of Hope and Fatalism shone through the lens of the Ragnarok myth.<br /> <br /> What has often proved to be a barrier has been the fact that these courts are treated as a kind of add-on to the seasonal courts. They are fascinating, and have the capacity for depth but they on their own cannot a freehold make. So I sat down and I came up with a seed of an idea to make a court system using Dawn and Dusk that would lead to a playable freehold court system.<br /> <br /> I've got some ideas but was hoping that the board can help me play with these ideas:<br /> <br /> The core of this court system is that Dawn and Dusk represent not just the Ragnarok myth, but also the Aesir and their more warlike tendencies. It occured to me that a good counterpoint might be to make two additional courts using the themes of a Couple Vanir, and be the ones who functionally make a freehold stable while the two more warlike courts are out there being more active.<br /> <br /> <u>The Courts</u><br /> Dawn<br /> Emotion: Hope<br /> Patron God: Baldur<br /> Theme: Mostly As Per Swords at Dawn.<br /> Exploring the more mystical aspects of Death is definately in their thematic purview<br /> <br /> Dusk<br /> Emotion: Fatalism<br /> Patron God: Odin<br /> Theme: Mostly As per Dancers at Dusk.<br /> An added theme worth exploring is also revitalization.<br /> <br /> Day<br /> Emotion: Belonging<br /> Patron God: Freya<br /> Theme: Fertility, Community, Passion, Healing, Attraction, Beauty<br /> <br /> Night<br /> Emotion: Security<br /> Patron God: Heimdall<br /> Theme: Awareness, Guardianship, Protection, Forwarning, Travel<br /> <br /> <br /> Groupings:<br /> Dusk and Dawn as Courts of Battle<br /> -Their emotions are the two sides of the Ragnarok myth: The Fatalism of its inevitability and the Hope of knowing that something worthwhile will come after.<br /> Day and Night as Courts of the Homestead<br /> -Their emotions are both related to the comfort of community, both the sense of Belonging to something greater and the Safety that numbers bring.<br /> <br /> Freehold roles:<br /> Dusk: Tears down<br /> Dawn: Builds up<br /> Day: Maintains Morale<br /> Night: Watches for Danger<br /> <br /> Dusk is about Fighting despite the odds, Dawn is about Winning despite the odds.<br /> Day is about the stabilizing effect community has, Night is about Keeping that community safe.<br /> Dawn is about growing hope, Day is about having something to hope for.<br /> Dusk is about the Inevitability of loss, Night is about Minimizing Damage.<br /> Dawn is about making a better tomorrow, Night is about making sure things don\u2019t slip backwards<br /> Dusk is about Fighting the good fight, Day is about making sure there\u2019s something worth fighting over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1838,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox","user":"danparadox","date":". 05-17-2017, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox","name":"danparadox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1838_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T05:06:10-07:00","id":1091484,"title":"","content":"I can see the Dawn and Dusk Courts being added to any court system. <br /> <br /> I'd think it'd be interesting if the Dawn and Dusk courts were Nomandic Courts that move from Freehold to Freehold based on events happening that draw them to a Freehold. <br /> <br /> So when the two Court joining ones Freehold is a sign of events to come, an Omen, but also a tool to survive and/prosper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T10:27:07-07:00","id":1091611,"title":"","content":"Aren't there already Slavic Day and Night courts? You might need another name for those courts to avoid confusion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T20:42:40-07:00","id":1091818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1091310-norse-courts-or-a-dude-trying-to-make-a-stable-freehold-with-dawn-and-dusk?p=1091611#post1091611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't there already Slavic Day and Night courts? You might need another name for those courts to avoid confusion</div> </div> </div> </div>Sun and Moon. Common mix-up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T03:14:28-07:00","id":1092289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1091310-norse-courts-or-a-dude-trying-to-make-a-stable-freehold-with-dawn-and-dusk?p=1091484#post1091484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see the Dawn and Dusk Courts being added to any court system.<br /> <br /> I'd think it'd be interesting if the Dawn and Dusk courts were Nomandic Courts that move from Freehold to Freehold based on events happening that draw them to a Freehold.<br /> <br /> So when the two Court joining ones Freehold is a sign of events to come, an Omen, but also a tool to survive and/prosper.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Technically, that is exactly what they are: Nomadic courts that go where the action is. <br /> The key thing is though, the courts don't exactly mesh with the courts one normally finds in a freehold, nor do they have a real write up when it comes to the nature of the court's political structures as is.<br /> <br /> What I'm curious is what people think of the combination, if the two I've added mesh well thematically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox","name":"danparadox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1838_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T05:14:50-07:00","id":1092750,"title":"","content":"I think a court dedicated to Freyja would be more about passion.<br /> She is a very emotional goddess. Weeps tears of gold over her lost husband, but sleeps with anything she wants to.<br /> She's commands fully half of the Einherjaren and an equal portion of Valkyries.<br /> She's also probably the greatest sorceress among the Vanir.<br /> <br /> Really, a court dedicated to Freyja would probably be some strange mixture of Autumn and Summer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T00:10:06-07:00","id":1093556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1091310-norse-courts-or-a-dude-trying-to-make-a-stable-freehold-with-dawn-and-dusk?p=1092750#post1092750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a court dedicated to Freyja would be more about passion.<br /> She is a very emotional goddess. Weeps tears of gold over her lost husband, but sleeps with anything she wants to.<br /> She's commands fully half of the Einherjaren and an equal portion of Valkyries.<br /> She's also probably the greatest sorceress among the Vanir.<br /> <br /> Really, a court dedicated to Freyja would probably be some strange mixture of Autumn and Summer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A good suggestion to add.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hmmm...any suggestions for alternative names for emotions?<br /> Wariness or Safety rather than Security for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1838,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox","user":"danparadox","date":". 05-17-2017, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox","name":"danparadox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1838_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T04:51:32-07:00","id":1093614,"title":"","content":"Oh! Another thing about Freyja.<br /> Her name literally means &quot;The Lady&quot;, and she is the queen of the bright elves.<br /> One tale about her talks about how she created war between two kings, placed them on an un-escapable island, and each night ressurects their fallen soldiers, so that their warring will go on until Ragnar\u00f6k.<br /> <br /> Really, one doesn't have to look far to see her, or for that matter, the All-Father as Gentry.<br /> If I were to place the Old Gods as anything in CofD, it'd be some kind of Fae. (Of course, I'd generally make them composite characters of lots of things, but my point still stands).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danparadox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1091310-norse-courts-or-a-dude-trying-to-make-a-stable-freehold-with-dawn-and-dusk?p=1093556#post1093556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A good suggestion to add.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hmmm...any suggestions for alternative names for emotions?<br /> Wariness or Safety rather than Security for example?</div> </div> </div> </div>Protection? Comfort?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T16:12:57-07:00","id":1099943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1091310-norse-courts-or-a-dude-trying-to-make-a-stable-freehold-with-dawn-and-dusk?p=1093614#post1093614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh! Another thing about Freyja.<br /> Her name literally means &quot;The Lady&quot;, and she is the queen of the bright elves.<br /> One tale about her talks about how she created war between two kings, placed them on an un-escapable island, and each night ressurects their fallen soldiers, so that their warring will go on until Ragnar\u00f6k.<br /> <br /> Really, one doesn't have to look far to see her, or for that matter, the All-Father as Gentry.<br /> If I were to place the Old Gods as anything in CofD, it'd be some kind of Fae. (Of course, I'd generally make them composite characters of lots of things, but my point still stands).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Protection? Comfort?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm aware that many of the Old Gods have their capricious natures, but I liked the idea of using aspects of their myths and personalities to theme courts, truth be told they can be dropped, but I like the idea that their myths help inspire as much as the seasons. <br /> <br /> &quot;Comfort&quot; I feel is a theme of the courts of the homestead, both Day and Night are about different aspects of comfort.<br /> Day is the comfort one derives from other people, from being a part of a community and knowing that the community supports you.<br /> Night is the comfort one has from knowing that you are protected. That the doors and windows are locked or that a child's parents watches over them as they sleep. <br /> Rather than being opposites these emotions are complementary.<br /> <br /> I keep finding people having trouble with &quot;fatalism&quot; as an emotion, I'd argue that the term &quot;resignation&quot; doesn't have the same oomph that &quot;hope&quot; does. But I also note that not all emotions are as passionate as others. One can inspire fatalism as much as one can inspire hope, it's the speeches delivered on the battlefield to soldiers that know they might be the ones to die, it's the acts of triage that are done by emergency medical practicioners, at the most mundane it's the teachers who have to encourage students to still seek their highest potential despite their circumstances(the latter I've seen too often as from a family of teachers). I suppose the issue is that fatalism is connected to a concept of self-sacrifice on a romantic level in stead of a more mundane understanding that a person is simply acting against the forces of entropy despite the fact that entropy will always win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox","name":"danparadox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1838_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T12:12:17-07:00","id":1101326,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, we're doing a writeup for Reykjavik in the core book. Our take is that there are seasonal groups there, but they symbolize different things and function differently on a magical level. And Icelandic Lost aren't fond of the word &quot;Court,&quot; either. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T12:28:25-07:00","id":1101338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1091310-norse-courts-or-a-dude-trying-to-make-a-stable-freehold-with-dawn-and-dusk?p=1101326#post1101326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, we're doing a writeup for Reykjavik in the core book. Our take is that there are seasonal groups there, but they symbolize different things and functio